export const SEQUENCE_REFERENCE = "=== The generator contract ===\n# Story sequence generator\n\nYou generate production-ready story sequences: the founder (or a client) picks a type or just says what they want to talk about; you shape it into the right sequence type, request the specific photos needed with concrete recommendations, and write the slide-by-slide copy.\n\n\n## Step 1 — intake\n\nIf the user named a type, use it. If they described an intent (\"a case study and how it relates to viewers\", \"how I never imagined getting here\"), map it yourself and confirm in one line. The type menu (Niksetting's own seven, from his corpus + captured caption):\n\n1. **Value-driven** — a story containing something genuinely useful; scene -> tension -> framework/lesson. Shows the level of thinking.\n2. **Credibility** — result stacking: open with a result, wins across the board, close with a positioning statement. (A \"case study\" intent usually lands here or in breakdown.)\n3. **Q&A** — question box; answer ~12h later; 50/50 technical/personal; write your own questions if too few arrive.\n4. **Day-in-the-life** — timestamped founder day; every slot carries value, education, or proof.\n5. **Breakdown** — teach one ICP topic step by step (educational; old way / new way frames).\n6. **Lifestyle** — the 20% human share; personal bonding. (For Pulsify: humanity without flex — see currency rule.)\n7. **CTA** — the conversion sequence; the 9-slide frame below.\n\nPer-type deployment (from the captured 964k carousel matrix — guide cadence and audience fit): value-driven 1-2x/week (demonstrates expertise, all niches); credibility 2-3x/week (instills trust, saturated niches); Q&A 1x/week (removes friction, skeptical audiences); day-in-the-life 1-2x/month (creates familiarity, B2C); breakdown 1x/week (justifies pricing, DWY/DFY offers); lifestyle 1-2x/week (creates desire - Pulsify serves this with mission/transformation, never possessions); CTA under 1x/month (tests demand - over-asking burns the audience).\nPlus the permanent assets: **start-here** (the 18-slide deployed architecture with the lesson template — the highlight's NAME is free per founder ruling: \"start here,\" \"new here?\", or anything that fits the account; likewise proof highlights may be named \"clients,\" \"student wins,\" \"results,\" and there can be several) and **story launch** (the ~9-slide stories webinar; only for accounts with accumulated sequence data).\n\nThen collect (ask only what's missing, in ONE message): who this is for (Pulsify or which client); the topic/angle in their words; the goal (reach vs DMs vs booked calls -> sets CTA placement); the trigger word if a hard CTA is wanted; available proof (results, receipts, screenshots — never invent any number or result); slide count preference (default 7-9).\n\n## Step 2 — request the photos (before or with the copy)\n\nFor every slide, specify the photo needed as a concrete, shootable request: shot type + setting + mood, with 1-2 realistic alternatives. Follow the captured visual grammar (wide frames where the environment argues, close-ups for authority moments, a warm register-drop at the close) but ALWAYS in Pulsify proof currency — founder-ratified: real workspaces, screen receipts, client dashboards, whiteboards/Miro, team calls, gym/walk humanity shots. Never cars, watches, hotels, cash. Phone-raw beats polished (ratified dial 4).\n\nExample of the expected specificity: \"Slide 3 (proof): screenshot of the client's Stripe/analytics dashboard, actual numbers visible, cropped to the chart — phone screenshot is fine. Alternative: the WhatsApp message where they told you the result, name blurred.\"\n\nIf the user already has photos, ask them to list/drop what they have and fit the sequence to the inventory rather than demanding reshoots.\n\n## Step 3 — generate\n\nEvery sequence walks the universal 6 steps: curiosity -> pain (call out the pain, not the situation) -> statement+proof -> belief shift (one reframe, driven deep) -> result -> close from abundance.\n\nFor conversion-goal sequences use the 9-slide frame: 1-3 pattern interrupt + proof/value thread; 4-6 pain mirror + the gap; 7-9 access, offer, CTA. Slides 1-6 are pure value — no pitch before slide 7. CTA dial (ratified): volume goal (lead magnet) = CTA on slide 1; qualification goal = CTA at the end. Engineered CTAs are primary doctrine — a soft CTA (lead magnet/long form) and/or a hard CTA (DM trigger word); never omit the ask on a conversion sequence.\n\nOutput format — one block per slide:\n\n```\nSLIDE n — {job in the 6-step arc}\nTEXT: the overlay copy, exactly as it should be typed (line breaks = separate pills)\nEMPHASIS: which words get underline/color/box and why\nPHOTO: the request from step 2 (+ alternative)\nINTERACTIVE: poll/question/link/none\n```\n\nThen: 2 alternative openers for slide 1 (the hook decides everything), a one-line \"why this order\" note, and the posting note (time-of-day free; sequences post as one run).\n\n## Copy rules (hard)\n\n- Pill-box style: short lines, one thought per pill, 1-3 pills per slide plus one quotable line where it earns it. Lowercase-casual is allowed for founder-voice accounts; match the account's captured register.\n- The reframe rule: one belief shift per sequence, repeated, not five.\n- The lesson template is available as a pattern: \"You might X / You might Y / But you don't have {deliverable} / '{quotable law}'.\"\n- Pain, not situation: \"you're tired of watching leads go cold\" not \"you make 20K/month\".\n- Real numbers only, from the supplied proof. If proof is thin, write a proof-light sequence (value/Q&A types) and SAY the credibility type needs receipts first.\n- Voice guard final pass: no negative parallelism spam, minimal em-dashes, no \"here's the kicker\", no curly quotes, no invented stats. Sentence-level read-aloud test: would the founder say this on camera?\n- Divide-by-three law: any revenue number in the copy attracts people earning about a third of it — calibrate aspirational numbers at ~3x the target client.\n\n\n\n=== The story sequence system (types, 6-step arc, 9-slide frame, CTA dial) ===\n# The story sequence system\n\nThe canonical Pulsify framework for Instagram story sequences: what they are, the five types, the universal slide structure, the daily 9-slide frame, the permanent assets (start-here, story launch), cadence, delegation, and measurement. Source is the Niksetting corpus (single-source, per [[synthesis/cross-creator-synthesis]]), cross-validated where SooWei's material touches it, with Pulsify deltas applied throughout. This page is the spec for the story-sequence generator.\n\n## Why this matters for Pulsify\n\nStories are the highest-trust surface on Instagram and the closing surface of the profile funnel: reels make strangers problem-aware, YouTube converts deep trust, stories close daily. The operating math: every watched story adds roughly 1% to conversion likelihood; a hundred watched stories makes a customer on average (range observed: 3 to 100). The people who buy are the silent daily-sequence watchers, not the reel engagers. Pulsify needs this system twice over: for its own profile and as a client deliverable inside the Content Engine.\n\n## What a story sequence is\n\nA designed multi-slide daily story arc where every slide earns the next one. The core mechanic: \"every next story adds value to the prior story,\" holding the viewer in a flow state until the sequence's job is done. Sequences are built for credibility and conversion, never for views; a deep sequence deliberately sheds casual viewers to concentrate buyers. Stories are also the safe surface: feed content can damage a brand, stories tolerate experiments.\n\n## The sequence types — reconciled canon\n\nNiksetting names his types in three places, and they don't fully overlap. The masterclass teaches FIVE (Q&A, educational, credibility, value-driven, lead magnet). Video 07 operates SEVEN frameworks (founder day-in-the-life, timeline-based, Q&A, client result stacking, no-idea day, story launch, lifestyle). His own carousel caption (captured 2026-07-11, the \"$964,853\" post: \"after analyzing the data of over 1,000 individual sequences, I found the 7 types that create the highest retention & profit\") lists his OFFICIAL SEVEN: **value-driven, credibility, Q&A, day-in-the-life, breakdown, lifestyle, CTA.**\n\nThe caption list is the newest and most considered; Pulsify adopts it as the canonical type menu, with the reconciliation map: educational = breakdown; client result stacking = credibility; lead magnet + timeline-based = CTA (the conversion-frame types); no-idea day = a fallback mode, not a type; story launch and start-here = permanent/campaign assets above the daily types.\n\n## The seven types (canonical), plus modes and assets\n\n1. **Value-driven.** A story that contains something genuinely useful: set a scene, build tension, walk through a framework or lesson. Goal: show your level of thinking and let them feel they got something for free. Visual quality is mandatory here; a value sequence with bad photos doesn't read as valuable.\n2. **Credibility (result stacking).** Open with a result, stack wins across the board, close with a positioning statement that doubles as a belief shift. Materials: screenshots, client messages, revenue dashboards. Sequence order is engineered association: an education slide first makes every result that follows feel like proof of that exact claim. One win is luck, three is a pattern, ten is undeniable; never stop stacking. **Pulsify delta:** proof currency is student results, transformation receipts, funded-account passes. Never watches, cars, or lifestyle (see [[concepts/trust-recession]]; SooWei's prediction that lifestyle marketing dies is the confirming source).\n3. **Q&A.** Open a question box; answer 12 hours later, picking the questions your ICP cares about. Balance answers 50/50 technical (delegable) and personal (founder-only). Cold-start rule: not enough questions, write your own — you know the pain points. The psychology: questions are the audience inviting you to perform your expertise; they want to see how you think, and every answer is a free consult. Run at least biweekly.\n4. **Day-in-the-life.** Timestamped documentation of a real founder day — but never bare documentation: every slot carries one of value, education, or proof. The deepest follow hook because the audience wants to replicate the founder's day. Simplified evergreen variant (photo + time only) trades conversions for views.\n5. **Breakdown (educational).** One ICP topic walked across ~6 slides, belief-shift framed (old way / new way). Lead with what they walk away with, never with what they'll learn: the outcome, not the process.\n6. **Lifestyle.** The 20% human share of the 80/20 rule: personal bonding, \"make sure your audience knows what you're up to.\" **Pulsify register:** humanity without flex — training, travel-as-context, food, the desk at 2am; never possessions as the subject.\n7. **CTA (conversion sequences).** The frames built to sell: timeline-based value-chaining (\"every next story adds value to the prior story\") ending in the ask, and lead magnet sequences (CTA on slide one, ends in the email list, taking the relationship off the algorithm; hook carries outcome + specificity + speed — \"the exact 12 hooks I used to make $4M in client revenue, yours in 30 seconds,\" never \"here's a PDF\").\n\nFallback mode, not a type: the **no-idea day** — 5-10 evergreen niche topics, deliberately structureless; the lack of structure itself reads as personal and builds trust.\n\n### The deployment matrix (cadence / function / audience per type)\n\nFrom his own \"$964,853\" carousel (\"after analyzing over 1,000 individual sequences\"), each type has a distinct cadence, a job, and a best-fit audience. Captured in full at [[content-engine/carousel-breakdowns/niksetting-964k-story-sequences]]. This is the when/why/for-whom layer the generator selects from:\n\n| Type | Cadence | Function | Best-fit audience/offer |\n|------|---------|----------|-------------------------|\n| Value-driven | 1-2x/week | Demonstrates expertise | All niches |\n| Credibility | 2-3x/week | Instills trust | Saturated niches (where claims are cheap) |\n| Q&A | 1x/week | Removes friction | Skeptical audiences |\n| Day-in-the-life | 1-2x/month | Creates familiarity | B2C niches |\n| Breakdown | 1x/week | Justifies pricing | DWY & DFY offers |\n| Lifestyle | 1-2x/week | Creates desire | Biz-opp offers |\n| CTA (conversion) | <1x/month | Tests demand | All niches |\n\nRead the totals: credibility is the workhorse (2-3x/week), value/breakdown/lifestyle mid-frequency, Q&A weekly, CTA rare (over-asking burns the audience), day-in-the-life sparing. A healthy week is credibility-heavy with value and breakdown support, Q&A weekly, a CTA only when demand is being tested. **Pulsify swap:** the lifestyle type's \"creates desire\" job is served by mission and transformation, not possessions; keep the cadence, change the currency.\n\n## The universal six-step slide structure\n\nEvery sequence, regardless of type, walks these steps:\n\n1. **Curiosity** — the pattern-interrupt open.\n2. **Obstacle** — name what blocks them; call out the pain, not the situation (\"are you making 50 grand a month\" is a situation; the reason they hate being there is the pain).\n3. **Statement + proof** — the claim, backed immediately.\n4. **Belief shift** — the frame transition; one reframe driven so deep they can't unhear it.\n5. **Result** — show the outcome and the trust it earns.\n6. **Close from abundance** — the ask, made like someone who doesn't need it.\n\nAfter a few weeks this stops being a checklist and becomes instinct.\n\n## The daily 9-slide frame\n\nThe default conversion sequence shape (from the Amer case, [[synthesis/niksetting-extractions/06-200k-months-amer-case-study]]):\n\n- **Slides 1-3:** pattern interrupt, then proof/value establishing the thread.\n- **Slides 4-6:** the pain mirror. Reflect their situation back until they feel it, then show the gap between their pain and the solution, so crossing it requires access to you.\n- **Slides 7-9:** access, offer, CTA. \n- Why it works: slides 1-6 are pure value, no pitch. By slide 7 they already feel the problem, so the offer lands as help, not selling.\n\n**CTA placement is a dial, not a rule:** volume goal (lead magnets) puts the CTA on slide 1 before drop-off eats reach; qualification goal puts it after slide 7, because whoever clicks there genuinely cares. Ask which you want before building.\n\n## Permanent assets\n\n- **Start-here sequence.** The first highlight on the profile, permanent, tapped first by every new visitor: the silent sales pitch. **Naming is free (founder ruling):** \"start here,\" \"new here?\", or B2C-friendly labels — the captured \"New here?\" is one example of the concept, not the required name. The same logic extends to the rest of the highlight rail: one or more proof highlights (\"clients,\" \"student wins,\" \"results 1/2/3\"), a mechanism highlight, an apply highlight — buckets per [[playbooks/instagram-growth-workstream]], names per account. Taught structure (10 slides): your story (3) -> client proof (3) -> the framework (2) -> the close (2). **Deployed reality (captured live, [[content-engine/sequence-breakdowns/niksetting-new-here]]):** his actual \"New here?\" runs 18 slides — hook+receipt, then a lesson/proof alternation, mechanism reveal, register-drop close, and dual CTAs (abundance first, scarcity appended a week later; the highlight accretes as a living asset). The reusable **lesson template** inside it: \"Lesson N: {one word}\" -> three \"You might...\" concessions -> \"But you don't have {a deliverable of the offer}\" -> a quotable law in quotes. Ten lessons = the offer's deliverables disguised as free education. Zero selling, purely the journey; each slide pairs a pain point with your insight from a belief perspective. Your story plus their pain points filters wrong-fit visitors automatically. **Pulsify note (founder-ratified):** start-here vs landing page is a per-audience test, not doctrine. Run both, measure where the audience interacts; if IG story interaction wins, the start-here carries conversion, otherwise the landing page does (the founder's prior: a landing page almost never fails). Cold outreach keeps pages regardless. Dial 5 in [[synthesis/cross-creator-synthesis]].\n- **Story launch.** A short webinar run in stories to sell something; ~9 slides. His numbers: $600K total from launches, $250K from one sequence at 71.9% completion. Launches are built from the account's own accumulated data, never copied — the structure transfers, the copy never does.\n- **Highlights.** Every well-performing sequence gets saved into its bucket ([[playbooks/instagram-growth-workstream]] buckets stand: My story, Start here, Results, Mechanism, Apply).\n\n## Cadence and delegation\n\n- Floor: 3 sequences per week. Target: 5-7 (near-daily). Practitioner level: daily. Slides per day: 3-7.\n- Weekly type mix to rotate: credibility, educational, value, Q&A (biweekly minimum), lead magnet, plus day-in-the-life or no-idea days as filler that still fits the system.\n- Delegation split: ~3 personal days a week the founder shoots from the phone; the team runs structured storylines the other days from a process they can follow. Full automation fails — the personal touch is the product and nobody can read the founder's mind. Technical/systematized content is delegable; personal is not.\n- Batch production kills the growth signal: audiences buy from people they watch grow, and week-old batches can't carry this week's growth.\n\n## Measurement\n\n- **Drop-off rate** is the only per-sequence metric that matters: the view gap between first and last slide. Leave at slide 2 = hook failed. Leave at slide 7 = body went sideways. Improve one percentage point at a time.\n- Track per sequence: views, completion %, DMs and interactions, profile visits, compared performance vs prior sequences. Log copy so winners are reusable. A VA can run the tracking; Claude can run the analysis.\n- Account-level dashboard: drop-off rate, opt-in rate, and (per source, undefined) save rate. Supplement with SooWei's weekly set: net follower growth, ICP leads gained, follower-to-view ratio, dollar-per-follower. Week-over-week comparisons only.\n- The 1%-per-story rule is a mnemonic, not a measurement: consistency makes the math inevitable, absence decays it (\"when you don't post story sequences, you decrease the conversion potential\").\n\n## How Pulsify uses this\n\n1. **Own profile first.** Run the weekly mix on Pulsify's IG; the tracking log doubles as the validation data for the generator.\n2. **Client deliverable.** The system slots into the Content Engine component: per-client sequence calendar, type mix, delegation split, and the drop-off report in the monthly recap (mirrors the dashboard-product vision).\n3. **The generator.** This page is the spec: inputs are creator profile + sequence type + topic/goal; output is slide-by-slide copy (overlay text, visual direction, which of the six steps each slide executes) with CTA placement per goal and two hook variants. Voice rules apply; the humanizer pass runs on every output.\n\n## Connections\n\n- [[concepts/profile-funnel]] — the surface this system closes for.\n- [[synthesis/cross-creator-synthesis]] — the law/contested filter this page inherits.\n- [[synthesis/niksetting-extractions/07-story-sequences-7-frameworks]] and [[synthesis/niksetting-extractions/06-200k-months-amer-case-study]] — the primary sources.\n- [[content-engine/copy-voice-guide]] — the final pass on all generated slide copy.\n- [[playbooks/instagram-growth-workstream]] — the workstream this un-parks.\n\n## Open questions / gaps\n\n- Save rate: named in the source dashboard, never defined. Pending definition or replacement.\n- Slides 1-3 of the 9-slide frame are the least specified part of the source material; the generator should treat them as flexible (pattern interrupt + proof/value) until our own data says more.\n- Cadence numbers are the source's, not yet ours; first 30 days on Pulsify's own profile are the calibration run.\n- The visual layer (what winning slides actually look like) awaits the founder's screenshot ingestion.\n\n## Source trail\n\n- All Niksetting extraction pages cited in frontmatter; every claim traces to founder-supplied verbatim transcripts at `raw-sources/transcripts/niksetting/`.\n\n=== Worked example: a real high-performing sequence broken down slide by slide. Match its texture (pill length, emphasis, where proof sits). Never copy its words or its niche ===\n# Niksetting — \"New here?\" highlight — the start-here sequence in the wild\n\n**Sequence type:** start-here (delivered as a \"10 lessons\" educational spine with proof interludes)\n**Slides:** 18 captured (slides 1-17 posted ~27 weeks ago, slide 18 added a week later — highlights accrete) | **CTA position:** slides 17-18 (end) | **Goal read:** qualification\n**One-line read:** his permanent silent sales pitch: a rags-to-riches hook, ten lessons that each name a pain his offer solves, proof interludes with full funnel receipts, and a soft two-stage CTA — the entire Grow Acquisition offer taught as free lessons.\n\nThis is the single most important capture so far: the actual start-here sequence from the man who teaches start-here sequences. Note immediately that the REAL structure is richer than his taught 10-slide template (story 3 / proof 3 / framework 2 / close 2): in practice he runs 18 slides on a lesson-proof alternation. Both live in [[frameworks/story-sequence-system]] now.\n\n---\n\n## Slide 1 — the hook\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/01 (014344).png]]\n\n- **Text (verbatim):** \"December 1-31st, 2022, i made $1,200/mo working as a roofer.\" / \"December 1-31st, 2025, made $316,670/mo selling a simple consulting offer.\" / \"These are the only 10 lessons i wish i knew before i started.\"\n- **Emphasis:** black pill-boxes on white text; the two mirrored December lines create the before/after; lowercase \"i\" throughout (intentional casualness).\n- **Proof widget:** an embedded revenue dashboard screenshot — \"Gross revenue $316,670.00 +$78,209.00\" with a daily chart Dec 1-31 2025. The claim and its receipt on the same slide.\n- **Visual:** luxury duplex penthouse living room, him small in frame at the window overlooking a city skyline, back turned. Mood: quiet-arrival aspiration. Wealth register: luxurious (real estate, not objects). Production: composed, likely shot by a second person. Sync: \"roofer to $316K\" against a penthouse — perfectly congruent.\n- **Slide job:** curiosity + statement/proof fused. The \"only 10 lessons\" line is the open loop for the whole sequence.\n\n## Slide 2 — Lesson 1: Quality\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/02 (014348).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 1: Quality\" / \"You might have views. You might have engagement. You might have nothing.\" / \"But you don't have a 100k audience of buyers that are capital rich, educated & ready-to-buy.\" / \"'You can make $50,000/mo in sales with a following of 500 people if you understand \"conversion\".'\" / \"Attention without intention is noise.\"\n- **Pattern note:** this is the LESSON TEMPLATE used ten times: title -> three \"You might...\" concessions -> \"But you don't have...\" (the pain, which is precisely a deliverable of his offer) -> a quotable law in quotation marks.\n- **Visual:** upscale restaurant dinner, him in a suit mid-conversation at a table of well-dressed people, massive pink art screens behind. Mood: elevated social proof, being-in-the-room. Wealth register: luxurious. Sync: \"capital rich, educated\" audience claim over a frame of exactly such people.\n- **Slide job:** obstacle/pain (views without buyers).\n\n## Slide 3 — proof interlude: the profile funnel receipt\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/03 (014351).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Grew 83,000 'NICHE' followers in 12 months\" (white card, NICHE in red caps and quotes) / green check \"The Profile Funnel\" (green underline) vs red X \"No strategy\" (red underline).\n- **Composition:** two stacked profile screenshots of HIS OWN account — after: 31 posts / 100K followers / bio \"Founder & CEO @growacquisition, DM me 'INFO'... The Profile Funnel(tm)\"; before: 27 posts / 17,2K followers / older bio. A hand-drawn blue arrow curves from the before to the after. Black background, no photo.\n- **Slide job:** statement + proof for the mechanism itself (and a masterclass in before/after self-receipts: same person, same handle, different strategy).\n- **Note:** the trigger word in his live bio is \"INFO\"; the sequence's own CTAs use different words — trigger words are per-asset, not global.\n\n## Slide 4 — Lesson 2: Predictability\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/04 (014355).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 2: Predictability\" / \"You might run ads. You might have gotten some clients from it. You might only have lost money.\" / \"But you don't have a way to predictably get 300 qualified followers a day that turn into high-ticket clients daily.\" / \"'When you can predict, you can scale'.\"\n- **Visual:** ornate hotel lounge (painted ceilings, backlit amber bar), him seated in black-on-black suit looking at his phone, water glass on the table. Mood: unbothered operator in old-money surroundings. Wealth register: luxurious. Production: composed candid.\n- **Slide job:** pain (unpredictable acquisition).\n\n## Slide 5 — proof interlude: the December ad funnel, fully naked\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/05 (014401).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"ONE simple Profile + Story ad strategy that is printing leads\" (ONE in red) / hand-scribbled red box: \"I spent $17,932 on ads, in December\" / then the full waterfall in white pills: \"Profile visits: 41,320 / Ad Followers: 2971 / Qualified Ad Followers: 1733 / Conversations Ads: 980 / Calls Booked Ads: 114 / Calls Completed Ads: 80 / Call Show Ups: 64 / Collected Ads: $162,100 / Collected Organic: $92,400 / Collected Back-End: $62,170 / Total December: $316,670.\"\n- **Background:** his actual notifications feed — a wall of \"started following you from your ad\" alerts with real accounts — plus an ad-spend dashboard screenshot (63,511 in local currency).\n- **Slide job:** proof at maximum depth. This is the densest dwell slide in the sequence (a genuine tap-hold slide) and the single best example of radical-transparency proof in the corpus: spend, every funnel stage, and the revenue split (ads/organic/backend) reconciling exactly to the slide-1 number.\n- **Note for the vault:** collected organic + backend > half the ad-attributed total; the ads feed the profile funnel, matching [[synthesis/niksetting-extractions/15-marketing-ecosystem-pull-vs-push]].\n\n## Slide 6 — Lesson 3: Outsource\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/06 (014406).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 3: Outsource\" / \"Now you run ads. Now you make content. Have 100's of lead coming in daily...\" / \"But you don't have a A-player setter in the DM's converting these leads into booked meetings.\" / \"'If someone else can do it 80% as good, they should do it 100% of the time.'\"\n- **Visual:** Dubai penthouse (Ain wheel + Palm visible through floor-to-ceiling windows), him standing small in a vast living room, shot from a mezzanine above. Mood: scale/altitude. Wealth register: luxurious. Sync: outsourcing/leverage message over a view that says \"I bought back my time.\"\n- **Slide job:** pain (no setter).\n\n## Slide 7 — proof interlude: talent acquisition receipt\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/07 (014413).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"I was lucky because the same ad strategy we use to acquire clients, we started using to acquire talent.\" / \"$300 spent, 74 applications, 1 A-player setter[,] now closed over $1.3M in sales for us within 6 months.\" / \"Same way i hired my closer & CSM.\" / \"Less than $1k total, 3 A-players, $3M+ impact.\"\n- **Visual:** long team/community dinner table at night, waterfront villa terrace, Aperol spritzes, laughter, a boom mic visible at frame edge (they film their own dinners). Mood: family/tribe celebration. Wealth register: elevated (experiences, not objects). Sync: hiring story over a frame of the actual team.\n- **Slide job:** proof + a second offer surface (they place setters — cf. the setter-management upsell in SooWei's corpus and his own acquisition tier).\n\n## Slide 8 — Lesson 4: Tracking\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/08 (014418).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 4: Tracking\" / \"You know your revenue. You know your ad spend. You might know some conversion rates.\" / \"But you don't have real-time visibility into every leak in your funnel costing you 6-figures in hidden revenue.\" / \"'Fix what exists before you scale what's broken.'\"\n- **Visual:** night street in Dubai (Burj Khalifa behind), matte-black Porsche 911 GT3, him in white leaning on it — and a giant glowing purple MOCHI MASCOT decal/projection on the car door (kawaii octopus face). Mood: flex fused with brand mascot playfulness. Wealth register: maximal. Production: professionally shot/edited composite.\n- **Slide job:** pain (tracking) — deliberately staged on the product's mascot (see slide 9).\n\n## Slide 9 — the Mochi reveal\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/09 (014421).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"I've spend a year building my buddy Mochi.\" / \"That tracks every conversion point from follower to client.\" / \"Every lead, every dm, every ad, every follow-up, every no show, so i knew my next move.\" / \"It works 24/7, 'built once, no salary, no turnover.'\" / \"Add Mochi to a good offer, profitable ads, a setter and you'll 3x your revenue in weeks.\"\n- **Visual:** him on stage with a mic presenting to a seated audience; the screen behind reads \"G profile x mochi\" with product UI mockups. Mood: authority/keynote. Production: professional event photography.\n- **Slide job:** mechanism reveal + product placement.\n- **VAULT RESOLUTION:** this closes the open \"Machi\" question from [[synthesis/niksetting-extractions/16-content-impossible-to-skip]] — the software is **Mochi**, his funnel-tracking product (profile x mochi), mascot: the purple plush. The \"$100K MRR month one\" claim from video 16 refers to this. It is ALSO the tracking system behind 07/11's dashboards, and the plushies in slide 14's Porsche frunk are the brand motif recurring.\n\n## Slide 10 — Lesson 5: Offer\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/10 (014426).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 5: Offer\" / \"You might have a service. You might charge $2k-$5k. You might struggle to close high-ticket.\" / \"But you don't have an offer positioned so clearly that people pay $5k-30k upfront without hesitation.\" / \"'If they question your price, you haven't communicated your value'.\"\n- **Visual:** foreground: a hand holding a phone showing a blurred DM inbox absolutely full of unread conversations (blue dots). Background: dim upscale venue, him gesturing. Mood: abundance-of-demand. The blur on the DMs is deliberate (privacy + intrigue). Right-aligned text pills (only slide so far with right alignment — variety inside the system).\n- **Slide job:** pain (offer positioning), with the inbox as ambient proof.\n\n## Slide 11 — Lesson 6: Profit Margin\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/11 (014431).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 6: Profit Margin\" / \"Most people tell you they make $500k/year. What they don't tell you is they take home $60k.\" / \"The info business model is good for one thing: cashflow and profit.\" / \"Don't overcomplicate it.\" / \"Make a shit load of money and keep your expenses low.\"\n- **Visual:** dusk aerial of a hillside glass villa, him alone at a long stone table with a laptop, warm interior light. Mood: serene solo-operator wealth. Wealth register: luxurious. Sync: \"keep expenses low\" over a villa — the one visibly incongruent frame (flagged in the dissection).\n- **Slide job:** belief shift (revenue vs take-home).\n\n## Slide 12 — Lesson 7: Identity\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/12 (014437).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 7: Identity\" / \"Don't compete on being better.\" / \"Compete on what others can't copy.\" / \"Unique positioning. unique content & custom delivery.\" / \"'If they can replicate it in 30 days, it's not an advantage'.\"\n- **Visual:** golden-hour infinity pool, him walking the pool edge, foreground desk with open laptop, glasses, notebook — work-and-paradise composition. Mood: earned freedom. Wealth register: luxurious.\n- **Slide job:** belief shift (category of one, compressed to story format).\n\n## Slide 13 — Lesson 8: Messaging\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/13 (014441).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 8: Messaging\" / \"What you verbally say needs to make sense with what you visually show.\" / \"When there's misalignment, their brain has to bridge the gap leading to friction.\" / \"When your words and visuals align, prospects instantly flow into what actually matters.\" / \"No friction leads to sales, always.\"\n- **Visual:** first-class airline cabin (burl wood, lamp, AirPods Max, MacBook on the tray). Mood: elite in-transit. Wealth register: maximal.\n- **Slide job:** belief shift — and deliberately self-referential: the verbal-visual law stated on a slide whose visual is the claim (\"my words about wealth align with what you see\").\n\n## Slide 14 — Lesson 9: Productivity\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/14 (014446).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 9: Productivity\" / \"You probably work on 100 things.\" / \"3 of them generate 80% of your results.\" / \"The other 97 make you feel productive.\" / \"Busy doesn't mean productive. Focus does.\" / \"Find the 3, remove the 97.\"\n- **Visual:** the Porsche's open frunk stuffed with purple Mochi plushies around a silver Rimowa case. Mood: playful flex; the mascot as running gag. Production: staged product shot.\n- **Slide job:** belief shift + brand-motif reinforcement (Mochi again — the product never leaves the frame for long).\n\n## Slide 15 — Lesson 10: Visibility\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/15 (014451).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"Lesson 10: Visibility\" / \"No one knows you exist.\" / \"And they won't unless you get your face out there.\" / \"You can have the best offer in the world. The best results in your industry. The best service delivery.\" / \"But if no one sees you, none of it matters.\" / \"Obscurity kills more businesses than bad services.\" / \"Get visible or forgotten.\"\n- **Visual:** professional podcast studio (softboxes, mics, skyline window), him being interviewed. Right-aligned pills. Mood: media-figure authority. Sync: visibility lesson inside a visibility apparatus.\n- **Slide job:** pain + belief shift, sets up the close.\n\n## Slide 16 — the close\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/16 (014455).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"The best part is I didn't just learn these lessons.\" / \"I packaged them into a repeatable process.\" / \"That process generated $4M for me and $85M for my clients in 3 years.\" / \"I know the blueprint required to build and scale any consulting offer from $0 to millions, most likely in your exact niche.\" / \"Multiple things work, but only one is the fastest and i chose to adapt that model.\"\n- **Visual:** daylight countryside dining table, him in a cap with a woman beside him, homey and warm — the ONLY soft/domestic frame in the sequence, placed exactly at the close. Mood: grounded, human, trustworthy. Deliberate register drop before the ask.\n- **Slide job:** result -> transition to close (\"most likely in your exact niche\" pre-handles THE objection per [[synthesis/niksetting-extractions/21a-masterclass-part-1]]).\n\n## Slide 17 — CTA one\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/17 (014459).png]]\n\n- **Text:** \"And listen, i'm not here to sell you anything[,] i want you to sell yourself.\" / \"'The right time', is the moment you feel ready to execute and utilize a NEW acquisiton [sic] strategy that no one else is using.\" / \"The proof is in the results you've already seen.\" / \"If you need 45-min to help me shape your vision into a product that scales...\" / \"reply 'gameplan' and we will get on a call to map out your custom roadmap and see if this fits your exact niche.\"\n- **Visual:** a smiling team member (young, casual) in a luxury mall (Cartier signage) holding an Apple bag and a new iPhone box. Mood: generosity/celebration — the company takes care of its people. NOT a founder shot: de-centering at the ask.\n- **Slide job:** close from abundance (\"not here to sell you anything\") + trigger word CTA (\"gameplan\"), qualification-gated (45-min, \"see if this fits your exact niche\").\n\n## Slide 18 — CTA two (added ~a week later)\n\n![[raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/18 (014516).png]]\n\n- **Text (10 rapid pills):** \"You know that we're actually the same.\" / \"we both have skills, i just took my skill and 'placed it in a better model'.\" / \"that's why you make $20k/mo, and i make $300k/mo.\" / \"reading this it probably makes you frustrated.\" / \"and i get it.. how? why? what do i do?\" / \"it just requires ONE framework. Best part it's free, seems simple..\" / \"but with all the free information out there, you probably won't find it, unless you search for 500 hours.\" / \"but i got you.\" / \"got 3 hours free tomorrow, reply 'ME' and i'll show you how to use this model as the 'leveraged' path.\" / \"an hour each, 3 spots, happy to help [red heart]\" / bottom: \"recently had a musician making $2k/mo join, now she's making $70k/mo with her musician offer.\" / \"If she can do it, you can too.\"\n- **Visual:** same restaurant frame as slide 2 (asset reuse across slides — photos are a bank, not one-offs).\n- **Slide job:** a second, scarcer CTA: same-as-you relatability -> belief shift (\"better model\", verbatim from [[synthesis/niksetting-extractions/06-200k-months-amer-case-study]]'s skill/model/market equation) -> real scarcity (3 spots, tomorrow, 1 hour each) -> a relatable floor-case (musician $2K->$70K widens the niche door the lesson slides may have narrowed).\n- **Note:** 26w vs 27w timestamps prove the highlight accretes — the start-here is a living asset, extended with fresh CTAs without rebuilding.\n\n---\n\n## Sequence dissection\n\n- **Structure map (actual, 18 slides):** hook+proof (1) -> [lesson-pain (2,4,6,8,10) alternating with proof interludes (3,5,7) and mechanism reveal (9)] -> belief-shift lessons (11-15) -> result/close (16) -> CTA from abundance (17) -> scarcity CTA appended later (18). The taught 10-slide template is the skeleton; the deployed version doubles it with proof interludes and dual CTAs.\n- **The lesson template (reusable):** \"Lesson N: {one word}\" -> three \"You might...\" concessions (meeting the viewer where they are, exactly the masterclass's stage-empathy) -> \"But you don't have {the precise deliverable of his offer}\" -> a quotable law in quotes. Ten lessons = ten offer deliverables disguised as education. This IS \"sell the vacation, name the pain\" executed slide by slide.\n- **Emphasis grammar:** black pill-boxes/white text as the default voice; white box + red word for proof headlines; red hand-drawn scribbles for spend receipts; green check/red X + underlines for before/after; quotes always around the \"law\" line; lowercase \"i\" everywhere. Alignment flips (left/right) to fit the photo's negative space.\n- **Visual grammar:** one luxury frame per slide, rotating registers — real estate (1,6,11,12), fine dining/social (2,10,18), old-money hotel (4), team/tribe (7,16,17), stage/media (9,15), travel (13), supercar+mascot (8,14). The founder appears small-in-frame in wide luxury shots (the wealth is the subject, he inhabits it) and close-up only in authority frames (stage, podcast). Register drops to warm/domestic exactly at the close. Mochi's purple mascot recurs as the single playful thread through the flex.\n- **Wealth register verdict:** maximal, unapologetic lifestyle proof — penthouses, GT3, first class. This is the largest single divergence from Pulsify doctrine in the entire capture set, and it coexists with his taught \"value beats lifestyle\" positioning. His resolution (from video 02/10): visible brand growth itself converts, and numbers/lifestyle are early-stage credibility scaffolding. **Pulsify's adaptation:** keep every structural element (lesson template, proof interludes, receipt density, register drop at close, dual CTA) and swap the visual currency: student dashboards, build screenshots, client calls, real workspaces. The one incongruent frame (slide 11: \"keep expenses low\" over a villa) shows why our currency is actually safer — his sync law violated by his own flex.\n- **Proof density is the real weapon:** slide 5's naked funnel (spend -> every stage -> revenue split reconciling to the hook's number) does more selling than any lifestyle frame. That is directly portable to Pulsify with our tracking data.\n- **What Pulsify adapts immediately:** the 18-slide start-here architecture for our own IG (per the ratified test doctrine, measured against the landing page); the lesson template as a generator pattern; the appended-CTA practice (living highlight); asset-bank reuse of photos.\n- **Feeds back to:** [[frameworks/story-sequence-system]] (start-here section updated: taught template vs deployed reality; lesson template added), [[synthesis/cross-creator-synthesis]] (Machi->Mochi resolved).\n\n## Source trail\n\n- 18 screenshots, founder-captured 2026-07-11, filed at `raw-sources/inspiration/story-sequences/niksetting/new-here/` (original capture timestamps preserved in filenames).\n\n=== Voice guide: check every line against it before answering ===\n# Copy voice guide — AI tells to avoid\n\nThe canonical standard for how Pulsify writes. Governs every word that leaves the building or gets published: outreach DMs, Loom scripts, VSLs, emails, landing page copy, YouTube scripts, and the wiki itself. It sits on top of the positioning rules in [[content-engine/packaging-rules]] and the asset rules in [[raw-sources/prompts/outreach-asset-prompt]] — those decide *what* to say, this decides *how it reads*.\n\nSourced from the AI-writing-tropes list (tropes.fyi by ossama.is), filtered and adapted to Pulsify's copy. Not every trope in the original applies to short sales copy; what is kept here is what actually shows up in DMs, scripts, and pages.\n\n## Why this matters for Pulsify\n\nThe entire brand is raw, authentic, human — a real operator who watched your content and diagnosed your business. The moment a prospect smells a templated AI message, that positioning collapses and the message reads as spray-and-pray. In a trust recession, an AI tell is the same trust-killer as an income-screenshot thumbnail: it signals low effort and a sale being run on you. Every pattern below is a tell. Removing them is not stylistic polish, it is the difference between \"this person studied me\" and \"this is bot #4000 today.\"\n\n## Scope — what this governs and what it does not\n\nGoverns the prose mechanics of all outbound and published copy, plus wiki prose.\n\nDoes **not** override two things:\n- **YouTube title packaging.** The [[content-engine/packaging-rules]] and the titles-thumbnails skill mandate a punchy, parenthetical-kicker title format on purpose. Titles are a validated format, not prose. Leave them alone.\n- **Internal reference scannability.** Bold-lead bullets and tight fragments are fine in internal wiki/SOP docs built for fast scanning. The bans below apply to *copy a human reads as writing* — DMs, scripts, VSLs, emails, pages, and any wiki *prose* paragraphs.\n\n## The principle: one is fine, ten is slop\n\nNone of these devices are banned outright. A single deliberate \"you don't need more leads, you need a system\" can land in a VSL. The tell is *reflex and volume* — the model reaching for the same move ten times because its training rewards it. Use a device when you choose it for effect. Never let it be the default shape every sentence falls into. If you cannot say why a device is there, cut it.\n\n## Word choice\n\n- **Magic adverbs.** Cut \"quietly,\" \"deeply,\" \"fundamentally,\" \"remarkably,\" \"arguably\" used to make a flat sentence feel profound. Say the thing plainly.\n- **AI vocabulary.** Drop \"delve,\" \"utilize\" (use \"use\"), \"leverage\" as a verb, \"robust,\" \"streamline,\" \"harness,\" \"seamless,\" \"certainly.\" These are dead giveaways.\n- **Ornate nouns.** No \"tapestry,\" \"landscape,\" \"paradigm,\" \"synergy,\" \"ecosystem,\" \"framework\" where a plain word works. \"The trading-content space,\" not \"the ever-evolving trading landscape.\"\n- **The copula dodge.** Use \"is\" and \"are.\" Stop replacing them with \"serves as,\" \"stands as,\" \"represents,\" \"marks.\" \"Nick's offer is the proof,\" not \"Nick's offer serves as the proof.\"\n\n## Sentence structure\n\n- **Negative parallelism (the #1 tell).** Kill \"It's not X — it's Y,\" \"not because X, but because Y,\" and \"The question isn't X. The question is Y.\" This is the single most recognizable AI shape. At most one per piece, chosen on purpose.\n- **The countdown.** No \"Not a bug. Not a feature. A design flaw.\" Stop negating two things to reveal a third.\n- **Rhetorical self-Q&A.** No \"The result? Devastating.\" Do not ask a question nobody posed just to answer it.\n- **Anaphora pile-ups.** Do not open three-plus sentences in a row the same way (\"They assume... They assume... They assume...\").\n- **Tricolon reflex.** One rule-of-three is elegant. Three rule-of-threes back to back is pattern failure. Vary the count.\n- **False ranges.** \"From X to Y\" only when there is a real spectrum with a middle. \"From innovation to transformation\" has nothing in between. Just name the two things.\n- **Filler transitions.** Cut \"it's worth noting,\" \"it bears mentioning,\" \"importantly,\" \"notably,\" \"interestingly.\" If it matters, just say it.\n- **Trailing \"-ing\" analysis.** No \"...highlighting its importance,\" \"...reflecting broader trends,\" \"...underscoring its role.\" These tack fake significance onto a plain fact.\n\n## Paragraph and format\n\n- **Fragment spray.** Stop chopping copy into one-thought-per-line fragments as standalone paragraphs for fake punch (\"He did it. Openly. In public.\"). Real people write in connected sentences. A fragment is a tool, not a default rhythm.\n- **Listicle in a trench coat.** Do not write a hidden list as \"The first... The second... The third...\" prose. Either write a real list or write real prose.\n- **Bold-lead bullets** (in prose/copy). Do not start every bullet with a bolded keyword and colon. Almost nobody writes by hand this way. (Internal scannable docs are exempt — see scope.)\n- **Em-dash addiction.** A human uses two or three em dashes in a piece, naturally. AI uses twenty. Default to commas, periods, or parentheses. This one is on me as much as anyone.\n- **Unicode decoration.** Type straight quotes (\"like this\"), not curly ones. Use \"->\" not the arrow glyph. No decorative unicode a person would not type.\n\n## Tone\n\n- **False suspense.** Cut \"here's the kicker,\" \"here's the thing,\" \"here's where it gets interesting,\" \"here's what most people miss.\" Deliver the point without the drumroll.\n- **Patronizing analogy.** Drop the reflexive \"think of it as...\" / \"it's like a...\". Explain the thing directly; reach for a metaphor only when it is genuinely clearer.\n- **\"Imagine a world where...\"** Skip the futurism invitation. State what changes.\n- **False vulnerability.** No performative \"and yes, I'll be honest...\" or \"this isn't a rant, it's a diagnosis.\" Real candor is specific and slightly uncomfortable, not a polished aside.\n- **\"The truth is simple.\"** Do not assert that a point is obvious, clear, or simple instead of proving it. If you have to say it is clear, it is not.\n- **Stakes inflation.** A DM about a funnel gap is not \"the defining shift of the decade.\" Keep the stakes the real size.\n- **Pedagogical voice.** Cut \"let's break this down,\" \"let's unpack,\" \"let's dive in.\" You are talking to an operator, not a classroom.\n- **Vague attributions.** No \"experts say,\" \"studies show,\" \"industry reports suggest.\" Name the source or cut the claim. (Reinforces CLAUDE.md: never invent a stat, never validate an unverified person.)\n- **Invented concept labels.** Do not coin \"the supervision paradox\" / \"the acceleration trap\" and use it as if it is a defined term. Naming a thing is not the same as making the argument.\n\n## Pre-send checklist (scan every asset for the top tells)\n\nBefore any DM, script, email, or page goes out, scan for these eight — they cover most of the damage:\n\n1. \"It's not X, it's Y\" negative parallelism — present? Cut to one or zero.\n2. Em dashes — more than three? Convert most to commas or periods.\n3. \"Here's the thing / here's the kicker\" — cut.\n4. \"Serves as / represents / stands as\" — replace with \"is.\"\n5. Bold-lead bullets in copy a person reads as writing — unbold.\n6. Curly quotes or arrow glyphs — replace with straight characters.\n7. Rule-of-three stacked more than once — vary it.\n8. \"It's worth noting / importantly / notably\" filler — delete.\n\n## How Pulsify uses this\n\nThis is now the default voice for everything the AI drafts. When generating any asset through [[raw-sources/prompts/outreach-asset-prompt]] or any other route, apply these rules in the final pass before output. When linting the wiki, flag prose pages that violate them. When a sales asset deliberately breaks a rule for effect, that is allowed once and on purpose — the ban is on the reflex, not the considered choice.\n\n## Connections\n\n- [[content-engine/packaging-rules]] — governs titles/thumbnails/hooks; this governs prose. The two do not overlap.\n- [[raw-sources/prompts/outreach-asset-prompt]] — decides what each asset says; this decides how it reads.\n- [[concepts/trust-recession]] — why an AI tell is a trust-killer in this market.\n\n## Open questions / gaps\n\n- The original tropes list targets long-form blog prose. Short sales copy (DMs, hooks) legitimately uses some punch the list discourages. The \"one is fine, ten is slop\" clause resolves most of this, but the line will sharpen as Pulsify's own sent copy accumulates reply-rate data.\n- No A/B data yet on whether de-AI'd outreach lifts reply rates for Pulsify specifically. Strong prior from the trust-recession thesis; confirm against real outreach numbers once volume exists.\n\n## Source trail\n\n- `C:\\Users\\Abdullah\\Downloads\\Humanizer AI Prompt.md` (AI writing tropes, sourced from tropes.fyi by ossama.is), ingested 2026-06-01.\n- [[content-engine/packaging-rules]], [[raw-sources/prompts/outreach-asset-prompt]] — existing writing governance cross-checked against the tropes list during integration.";
